    {
      "id": "claim_2ba24d07eaa34090a15ca4b0c96ae28b",
      "statement": "`TaskLogger` is the only sanctioned writer of `tasks.logs` and `status` from inside the worker; every `info/command/error/success` call performs a read-then-write of the JSONB `logs` array and any DB error is swallowed (the inline comment is explicit: \"Don't throw — we don't want logging failures to break the main process\"), so the logs array can be silently incomplete.",
