    {
      "id": "claim_415cf5064fa949dcba83046d584e00c4",
      "statement": "Single-task deletion is a soft delete (`UPDATE tasks SET deletedAt = now()`); bulk deletion via `DELETE /api/tasks?action=completed,failed,stopped` runs a real SQL `DELETE FROM tasks WHERE status IN (...) AND userId = ?` and returns the deleted rows — the two endpoints use opposite mechanisms and bulk delete is destructive and irreversible.",
      "evidence": [
