    {
      "id": "claim_7dbb59438c134694a769abec4c570020",
      "statement": "The worker is bounded by a `Promise.race` between `processTask(...)` and a `setTimeout` reject inside `processTaskWithTimeout`; when the timer wins, the timeout branch writes `status='error'` with message \"Task execution timed out. The operation took too long to complete.\" via `timeoutLogger.updateStatus('error', ...)` and clears the 1-minute warning timer — this timeout-driven `error` write is independent of the sandbox SDK timeout, which is a separate `maxDuration * 60_000` ms lifetime on the sandbox VM itself.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L252-L332",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:09ebd3fba65ce10d1756612f961d77ca4fb263f1357518ba4123ae7c8d906541:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://app/api/tasks/route.ts#L289-L332",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:c616fb2be1a1f27ee489c28e678d0e71d1609f4de3ae89d0712070cc05a367d6:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_71a1ef6a5d5d4ac8a1fced4a592305e5",
      "statement": "`POST /api/tasks` schedules the actual work inside a `next/server` `after(...)` callback (the inline comment: \"CRITICAL: Wrap in after() to ensure Vercel doesn't kill the function after response. Without this, serverless functions terminate immediately after sending the response.\"); because cookies and request-scoped state are unavailable inside `after()`, the handler must resolve `getUserApiKeys`, `getUserGitHubToken`, `getGitHubUser`, and `getMaxSandboxDuration` *before* entering the callback and pass them in as parameters.",
      "evidence": [
